required checks through locked command directives, provide follow-up patches, or signal\ndocs/architecture.md:193:review readiness. Repository build, test, format, and required-check commands run only through\ndocs/architecture.md:198:requesting the repository checks required by those instructions before reporting work done.\ndocs/architecture.md:199:Tracked file changes produced by locked commands remain pending for that patch agent until the agent\ndocs/architecture.md:200:commits them through the patch protocol or reverts them. Pending command changes block\ndocs/architecture.md:201:`@work-leaf done`, and the orchestrator returns the tracked diff so the agent can submit the command\ndocs/architecture.md:202:output as a provisional patch when it belongs in the final work.\ndocs/architecture.md:204:Review bookkeeping has three scopes. The controller records a launch-time review baseline for each\ndocs/architecture.md:205:patch agent, tracks the latest reviewed hash for that patch agent so the same agent head is not\ndocs/architecture.md:206:reviewed twice, and asks reviewers to inspect every provisional commit from the active baseline\ndocs/architecture.md:207:through the latest patch-agent commit. `CommandChat` also keeps the ordered exact review targets that\ndocs/architecture.md:208:completed review during the active instance, and those targets form the linearizer handoff. This lets\ndocs/architecture.md:209:one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier\ndocs/architecture.md:210:reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.\ndocs/architecture.md:213:system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command\ndocs/architecture.md:214:lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching\ndocs/architecture.md:215:one or more user agents. Multi-agent launch requests dispatch `new [prompt...]` once per requested\ndocs/architecture.md:225:- `send_command_agent_message` to route chat from the Work Leaf command surface to `command-agent`.\ndocs/architecture.md:227:- `start_review` to create or resume reviewer sessions for explicit history-wide review and stream\ndocs/architecture.md:228:  reviewer output.\ndocs/architecture.md:250:spawning, session naming, review lookup, loading bookkeeping, or orchestrator event routing.\ndocs/architecture.md:284:rendering invalidation, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends chat text to the selected\ndocs/architecture.md:286:newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits the buffered chat text.\ndocs/architecture.md:287:When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the chat buffer with\ndocs/architecture.md:288:`/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat\ndocs/architecture.md:292:state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready\ndocs/architecture.md:293:state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy\ndocs/architecture.md:302:  terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets\ndocs/architecture.md:316:command classification, `PatchCoordinator` for patch requests, and the active `AgentBackend` for\ndocs/architecture.md:326:`src/patch.rs::GitPatcher` validates and applies unified diffs under write locks and creates\ndocs/architecture.md:327:metadata commits for accepted patches. It also accepts a matching already-applied diff when a locked\ndocs/architecture.md:329:agent's provisional patch. `PatchCoordinator<B>` connects patch conflicts and malformed patch\ndocs/architecture.md:331:the public patch workflow types.\ndocs/architecture.md:333:`src/review.rs::GitHistory` reads latest agent commits from repository history, builds cumulative\ndocs/architecture.md:334:review targets for a patch agent since a launch or reviewed baseline, and resolves agent metadata\ndocs/architecture.md:335:commits by exact hash. `ReviewCoordinator<B>` launches reviewer agents against those review targets\ndocs/architecture.md:336:and loops until the reviewer reports no findings or the configured maximum round count is reached.\ndocs/architecture.md:337:`CommandChat` resolves reviewer `@work-leaf` directives, such as file reads, before interpreting\ndocs/architecture.md:338:reviewer output as findings. `CommandChat` and `WorkLeafController` keep a stable\ndocs/architecture.md:339:`review-<agent-id>` reviewer identity for each patch agent and skip latest agent heads that have\ndocs/architecture.md:340:already completed review. `AgentCommit`, `ReviewResult`, and `ReviewError` are the public review\ndocs/architecture.md:341:workflow types. `WorkLeafController` scopes automatic review after a patch agent reports done to the\ndocs/architecture.md:342:patch agent that produced the provisional commit; explicit review commands use the history-wide\ndocs/architecture.md:343:review target lookup.\ndocs/architecture.md:349:exact commits recorded as reviewed in the current command-chat or controller instance; unrelated\ndocs/architecture.md:350:historical agent metadata commits are outside the linearizer scope unless the user explicitly reviews\ndocs/architecture.md:351:or adds them in that session. When one patch-agent id completes multiple reviewed commits in one\ndocs/architecture.md:352:active instance, each reviewed hash is listed independently for the linearizer.\ndocs/architecture.md:357:`src/chat_title.rs` is crate-private. It builds the prompt used for hidden chat-title backend\ndocs/architecture.md:403:only be completed by changing documented ownership, dependency direction, extension boundaries, or\ndocs/architecture.md:405:same patch as the code change.\ndocs/architecture.md:425:existing test suites under `tests/orchestrator_protocol.rs`, `tests/patching.rs`,\ndocs/architecture.md:426:`tests/reviews.rs`, `tests/linearize.rs`, and `tests/workspace.rs` provide the current coverage\ntests/workspace.rs:17:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:18:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:52:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:53:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:69:            .any(|line| line.contains(\"unknown command chat command\"))\ntests/workspace.rs:82:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:83:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:101:            .any(|line| line.contains(\"unknown command chat command `/`\"))\ntests/workspace.rs:109:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:110:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:140:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:141:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:204:fn controller_uses_backend_agent_to_name_chat_from_first_prompt() {\ntests/workspace.rs:206:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend.clone());\ntests/workspace.rs:207:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:222:            && launch.feature == \"chat-title\"\ntests/workspace.rs:228:fn controller_uses_agent_profile_for_non_codex_launches_and_reviews() {\ntests/workspace.rs:229:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-custom-profile-review\");\ntests/workspace.rs:237:            \"UPDATE apply parser patch from user-1\",\ntests/workspace.rs:248:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_agent_profile(profile.clone());\ntests/workspace.rs:249:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:255:    controller.start_review().unwrap();\ntests/workspace.rs:267:            .any(|launch| { launch.id.as_str() == \"review-user-1\" && launch.kind == profile.kind })\ntests/workspace.rs:272:fn controller_starts_review_after_patch_agent_done_and_loops_until_clean() {\ntests/workspace.rs:273:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-automatic-review-loop\");\ntests/workspace.rs:278:        \"implemented patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:280:        \"FINDINGS\\n- missing reviewed wording\",\ntests/workspace.rs:281:        \"fixed review finding\\n@work-leaf patch address review\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-after\\n+after review\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:284:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root.clone(), backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:285:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:292:        \"after review\\n\"\ntests/workspace.rs:295:    let reviewer_id = AgentId::new(\"review-user-1\").unwrap();\ntests/workspace.rs:297:    let reviewer = snapshot\ntests/workspace.rs:298:        .session(&reviewer_id)\ntests/workspace.rs:299:        .expect(\"reviewer session exists\");\ntests/workspace.rs:300:    assert_eq!(reviewer.title, \"review user-agent\");\ntests/workspace.rs:301:    assert_eq!(reviewer.loading, None);\ntests/workspace.rs:302:    let patch_agent = snapshot.session(&agent_id).expect(\"patch agent exists\");\ntests/workspace.rs:304:        patch_agent\ntests/workspace.rs:307:            .any(|line| line.contains(\"missing reviewed wording\"))\ntests/workspace.rs:310:        patch_agent.lines.iter().any(|line| {\ntests/workspace.rs:311:            line.contains(\"user-1 reviewed by review-user-1: rounds=2 resolved=yes\")\ntests/workspace.rs:318:            && prompt.contains(\"missing reviewed wording\")\ntests/workspace.rs:319:            && prompt.contains(\"Please fix the patch\")\ntests/workspace.rs:322:        target == &reviewer_id\ntests/workspace.rs:324:            && prompt.contains(\"Please check the patch again\")\ntests/workspace.rs:329:fn controller_does_not_start_review_until_patch_agent_reports_done() {\ntests/workspace.rs:330:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-review-waits-for-done\");\ntests/workspace.rs:335:        \"implemented patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after\\n@work-leaf end\",\ntests/workspace.rs:339:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:340:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:348:            .session(&AgentId::new(\"review-user-1\").unwrap())\ntests/workspace.rs:350:        \"review must wait for the patch agent to report done\"\ntests/workspace.rs:352:    let patch_agent = snapshot.session(&agent_id).expect(\"patch agent exists\");\ntests/workspace.rs:353:    assert_eq!(patch_agent.loading, None);\ntests/workspace.rs:358:            .any(|launch| launch.id.as_str() == \"review-user-1\")\ntests/workspace.rs:363:            && prompt.contains(\"work-leaf patch applied\")\ntests/workspace.rs:364:            && prompt.contains(\"@work-leaf done\")\ntests/workspace.rs:369:fn controller_review_prompt_covers_all_agent_commits_since_launch() {\ntests/workspace.rs:370:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-review-full-agent-scope\");\ntests/workspace.rs:375:        \"first patch\\n@work-leaf patch first step\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after first\\n@work-leaf end\",\ntests/workspace.rs:376:        \"second patch\\n@work-leaf patch second step\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-after first\\n+after second\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:380:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:381:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:390:    let review_launch = launches\ntests/workspace.rs:392:        .find(|launch| launch.id.as_str() == \"review-user-1\")\ntests/workspace.rs:393:        .expect(\"reviewer launched\");\ntests/workspace.rs:395:        review_launch.prompt.contains(\"first step\"),\ntests/workspace.rs:397:        review_launch.prompt\ntests/workspace.rs:400:        review_launch.prompt.contains(\"second step\"),\ntests/workspace.rs:402:        review_launch.prompt\ntests/workspace.rs:407:fn controller_reuses_one_reviewer_for_repeated_patch_agent_iterations() {\ntests/workspace.rs:408:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-reuses-reviewer\");\ntests/workspace.rs:413:        \"first patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after first\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:416:        \"second patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme again\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-after first\\n+after second\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:420:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root.clone(), backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:421:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:435:    let reviewer_id = AgentId::new(\"review-user-1\").unwrap();\ntests/workspace.rs:440:            .filter(|launch| launch.id == reviewer_id)\ntests/workspace.rs:446:        target == &reviewer_id\ntests/workspace.rs:447:            && prompt.contains(\"Review the full patch scope\")\ntests/workspace.rs:453:fn controller_reviews_only_unreviewed_patch_agent_commits() {\ntests/workspace.rs:454:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-reviews-only-unreviewed\");\ntests/workspace.rs:460:        \"readme patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-readme before\\n+readme after\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:463:        \"changelog patch\\n@work-leaf patch update changelog\\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-changelog before\\n+changelog after\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:467:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:468:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:482:            .filter(|launch| launch.id.as_str() == \"review-user-1\")\ntests/workspace.rs:489:            .filter(|launch| launch.id.as_str() == \"review-user-2\")\ntests/workspace.rs:496:fn controller_auto_review_ignores_historical_agents_outside_current_patch_agent() {\ntests/workspace.rs:497:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-auto-review-current-agent-only\");\ntests/workspace.rs:513:                \"UPDATE apply historical patch\",\ntests/workspace.rs:516:                    \"Agent-ID: {old_agent}\\nFeature: historical\\nReason: previous work\\nContext: old patch\"\ntests/workspace.rs:525:        \"live patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:529:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:530:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:540:            .filter(|launch| launch.id.as_str().starts_with(\"review-\"))\ntests/workspace.rs:543:        vec![\"review-user-1\".to_string()]\ntests/workspace.rs:548:fn controller_linearize_uses_only_commits_reviewed_in_this_session() {\ntests/workspace.rs:549:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-linearize-current-reviewed-only\");\ntests/workspace.rs:561:            \"UPDATE apply legacy patch from user-2\",\ntests/workspace.rs:567:        \"live patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:572:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:573:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:593:fn controller_linearize_keeps_multiple_reviewed_commits_from_same_agent() {\ntests/workspace.rs:594:    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-linearize-same-agent-multiple-reviewed\");\ntests/workspace.rs:599:        \"first patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme once\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after first\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:600:        \"summary: first reviewed change\",\ntests/workspace.rs:602:        \"second patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme twice\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-after first\\n+after second\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\ntests/workspace.rs:603:        \"summary: second reviewed change\",\ntests/workspace.rs:607:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend.clone()).with_max_review_rounds(4);\ntests/workspace.rs:608:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:614:        .send_message(&agent_id, \"make a second reviewed update\")\ntests/workspace.rs:662:    let chat = CommandChat::new(root.clone(), backend.clone());\ntests/workspace.rs:663:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:684:    let chat = CommandChat::new(PathBuf::from(\"/repo\"), backend);\ntests/workspace.rs:685:    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\ntests/workspace.rs:838:        \"chat-title\".to_string()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
